.TH BADAPPLESTEIN 1 "July 2026" "BadAppleStein 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
badapplestein \- reconstruct any video as a mosaic of source library pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B badapplestein
.RB [ build | encode ]
.RB [ options ]
.I input
.I output
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B badapplestein
reconstructs any video as a mosaic of pages from a source library of PDFs
and images.
The tool operates as a two\-stage pipeline:
.TP
.B arrange
Pattern\-match each video frame against the source library to find the best
page for each region.
.TP
.B render
Assemble the matched pages into an output video at the target resolution.
.PP
When invoked without a subcommand, the tool auto\-detects the input type and
runs the appropriate stage, or both stages when given raw inputs and a
destination.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B badapplestein build
.I sources_dir
.RB [ options ]
.br
Build a source library from a directory of PDFs and images.
Extracts multi\-resolution feature descriptors and writes
.B features.bin
and
.BR registry.bin .
See
.BR badapplestein-build (1).
.TP
.B badapplestein encode
.I input_video
.I output_video
.RB [ options ]
.br
Encode a video using a previously built source library.
Runs the arrange and render stages to produce the final mosaic output.
See
.BR badapplestein-encode (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-library " " \fIdir\fR
Path to the source library directory.
Default:
.BR ~/.badapplestein/library/ .
.TP
.BR \-\-preset " " \fIname\fR
Resolution preset.
Valid values:
.BR 8k ,
.BR 4k ,
.BR 1080p ,
.BR 720p .
.TP
.BR \-\-width " " \fIpx\fR
Output width in pixels.
Overrides the preset width.
.TP
.BR \-\-height " " \fIpx\fR
Output height in pixels.
Overrides the preset height.
.TP
.BR \-\-fps " " \fIn\fR
Output frames per second.
Defaults to the input video frame rate.
.TP
.BR \-\-codec " " \fIname\fR
Video codec for the output.
Options:
.BR prores ,
.BR h264 .
Auto\-detected when omitted.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-hw
Disable hardware acceleration.
Forces software encoding even when GPU codecs are available.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-frames " " \fIn\fR
Maximum number of frames to process.
Useful for quick previews.
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " " \fIn\fR
Number of worker threads.
Defaults to the number of available CPU cores.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-manifests
Retain intermediate manifest files after a successful encode.
Normally these are cleaned up automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print detailed progress and diagnostic information to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress all non\-error output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine\-readable JSON progress and status messages.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.badapplestein/library/
Default location for the source library.
Contains
.B features.bin
and
.BR registry.bin .
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a library from a folder of manga PDFs and scan images:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein build \-\-library ~/my\-library ~/sources/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encode a video at 4K using the default library:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-preset 4k input.mov output.mov
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quick preview at 720p, first 300 frames:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-preset 720p \-\-max\-frames 300 in.mp4 preview.mov
.fi
.RE
.PP
Encode with explicit resolution and software\-only encoding:
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-width 1920 \-\-height 1080 \-\-no\-hw \-\-codec h264 in.mp4 out.mp4
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build and encode in one pipeline (auto\-detect shortcut):
.PP
.RS
.nf
badapplestein encode \-\-library ~/my\-library \-\-preset 4k in.mp4 out.mov
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR badapplestein-build (1),
.BR badapplestein-encode (1)
